WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.600
Margate was among 101 towns from across&nbsp;
England selected to bid for funding from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.320
the government's Towns Fund Initiative. This&nbsp;
is a once-in-a-generation opportunity to invest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.640
in local projects, drive growth and improve&nbsp;
the environment for the benefit of the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.320
community. The Town Deal comes at an important&nbsp;
and exciting time in Margate's history. The town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.360
has faced its challenges over the last 50 years&nbsp;
and now is the time to come together to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:33.840
it has a thriving economy 365 days a year. At the&nbsp;
heart of the Town Deal is the town investment plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.040
which sets out a long-term vision and strategy for&nbsp;
Margate, the investment plan makes the case for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.960
29 million pound investment supporting projects&nbsp;
themed around four interlinking interventions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.760
These build on what makes Margate so special and&nbsp;
deliver change that will benefit local people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:56.160
and visitors for years to come. Margate's growing&nbsp;
creative and cultural economy is an opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.800
not to be missed the first intervention is&nbsp;
therefore a nine million pound investment in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.840
scaling Margate's creative production and skills.&nbsp;
It will establish a creative land trust to support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.240
projects stretching from the High Street to&nbsp;
the Theatre Royal, building spaces for creative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.160
production and education. Potential locations&nbsp;
include the former Marks and Spencers, Primark and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.360
other key sites within the High Street. Investment&nbsp;
will bring life back to the town centre linking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.120
the coast to the historic Hawley Square and&nbsp;
establishing a creative economic hub driving jobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:34.560
skills, education and engagement. In its heyday&nbsp;
Margate was known as a place for well-being and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.800
tourism. The second intervention is a 6.5 million&nbsp;
pound investment in coastal well-being to support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.160
projects across Margate's coastline creating&nbsp;
new and surprising experiences for visitors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.480
Establishing better links between the town&nbsp;
centre Northdown Road and the coastline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.440
will deliver an improved network of connections&nbsp;
and encourage people to explore beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:02.400
seafront. The third intervention focuses on public&nbsp;
realm and connections with a 4.5 million pound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.920
targeted investment in the town centre, coastline&nbsp;
and residential areas making it easier to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.360
around and improving visitor amenities. This will&nbsp;
better connect Northdown Road to the town centre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.480
and create attractive public spaces as well as&nbsp;
enhancing cycling and walking infrastructure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.920
Margate's past has a role to play in its future.&nbsp;
The fourth intervention is therefore a nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:29.120
million pound investment in well-loved heritage&nbsp;
assets and will help secure a sustainable future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.720
for the Dreamland cinema complex and the Winter&nbsp;
Gardens which benefits the wider town. It will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.840
create new enterprise and cultural spaces for&nbsp;
both visitors and the community. It will also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.480
support the development of feasibility plans for&nbsp;
the future of important landmarks including the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.640
Arlington Arcade the old Town Hall and the lido.&nbsp;
The town investment plan has now been submitted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.440
to the Ministry of Housing Communities and Local&nbsp;
Government. Thank you to everyone who took the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.480
time to get involved and share their views. We're&nbsp;
currently waiting to hear back from the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.200
and in the meantime the Town Deal board and&nbsp;
project team continue to work in partnership with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:11.360
stakeholders local businesses and the community.&nbsp;
You can read the town investment plan in full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:17.840
keep up to date with how the deal progresses and&nbsp;
sign up to receive news at margatetowndeal.co.uk

